<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saul</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as King Saul</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saul was, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, the first king of Israel, a man of the tribe of Benjamin anointed by the prophet Samuel who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibeah">Gibeah</a>, traditionally in the late eleventh century BCE. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philistines">Philistines</a>, Ammonites and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amalekites">Amalekites</a>, quarrelled with Samuel and with his commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a>, and died with his sons at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mount-gilboa">Battle of Mount Gilboa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saul.jpg" alt="Saul" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernst Josephson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saul_1878.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
